==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|stick<,,stuck> it out}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To [[persist]] or [[continue]] to the end.
#: ''Plenty of people begin the training, but few '''stick it out''' for the year or two necessary to become proficient.''
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-08-08|author={{w|Janan Ganesh}}|title=The oneness of Ron DeSantis and Rishi Sunak|journal={{w|Financial Times}}|url=https://www.ft.com/content/7016945a-2950-418a-9325-c87734c7a6c3|passage=It is not that I predict a plea deal for Trump to withdraw, or a new stinginess among donors who see his legal bills mounting, or a health scare. But DeSantis must look at the historic record and see that a big part of becoming president is just '''sticking it out'''.}}


